      ":question/problem": "Given that ${1, 2}^{N}$ denotes the set of all infinite sequences with elements from ${1, 2}$, complete the following reasoning:\n\nFor any subset $A$ of the set $N$, consider the function $f$ that maps $A$ to the sequence $(s_{1}, s_{2}, s_{3}, \u2026) \u2208 {1, 2}^{N}$ such that:\n$= 2$ {{field-1}} {{field-2}} {{field-3}}\nSince $f$ is a bijection from {{field-4}} onto ${1, 2}^{N}$, we have that\n$\\mid {1, 2}^{N}|=$ {{field-5}}."
